   "text": "**Core skills used.** *Controlling the centre*: White traded pieces, leaving Black the pawn centre. *Pawn breaks and levers*: 20.e4 attacked its front pawn. *Hanging pawns*: the c5 and d5 pair stood side by side; after ...fxe6 d5 was the target. By the engine at depth 16, White's edge stayed small, about 0.3 to 0.4 pawn, after 20.e4 with best play from Black. It grew to over a pawn only after Black's 20...d4 21.f4. 20.e4 was the engine's top choice, not a win by itself; that is evidence, not proof."
